author_final_remarks.value:
We thank all reviewers for their constructive feedback, insightful suggestions, and positive assessment of our work. In the rebuttal phase, we addressed the reviewers' comments by:

**(1)** Adding comparisons against a recent state-of-the-art time-series baseline (Sim-MTM) and showing that our robustness-aware pretraining scheme consistently outperforms it under sensor outages;

**(2)** Adding evaluations on an environmental sensing benchmark (Beijing PM10), confirming the applicability of our approach beyond the automotive domain;

**(3)** Evaluating performance under composite failures (1–4 simultaneous sensor dropouts), demonstrating consistent gains across complex failure scenarios;

**(4)** Including comparisons with physics-based Kalman filtering, demonstrating superior estimation without requiring a physical model;

**(5)** Clarifying our choice of failure modes, dataset selections, and methodological distinctions (e.g., from domain randomization).

We believe these revisions further demonstrate the robustness gains from our proposed pretraining scheme and its practical value for handling sensor failures.

